\ Wrong-delta verdicts at a memoized call site.
\
\ Kept out of the eager suite. A compiled forwarding word that passes a
\ stack-borne quotation to an annotated word raises no mismatch under
\ --compile=eager, on the build before the memo as well.

use "testing" ;

"Same call site, different quotations" test-section
\ `via` holds one call site for `at-site`. The first quotation fills that
\ site's entry. The second must still be walked and reported. The first then
\ passes again after the miss displaced it.
at-site: ( n quot: ( n -- n n ) -- n n ) [ call ] ;
via: ( n q -- n n ) [ at-site ] ;
5 [ dup ] via + 10 "first quotation at the site passes" assert=
[ 5 [ dup dup ] via ] "a different quotation at the same site is still checked" assert-error
5 [ dup ] via + 10 "the first quotation passes again after the miss" assert=

"Closure-owned argument with the wrong delta" test-section
\ A curry product never enters the memo, so both verdicts hold at the same
\ hot site.
5 1 [ drop dup ] curry via + 10 "curried quotation with the right delta passes" assert=
[ 5 1 [ drop ] curry via ] "curried quotation with the wrong delta is reported" assert-error
